",,True,-1,"/-- `map φ S` is a subgroup of `map φ T` if `S ≤ T`.

The image of the subgroup `S` under the homomorphism `φ` is a subgroup of the image of `T` under `φ`.

Note that `φ` does not need to be injective. So, in particular, even if two elements from `S` are mapped to the same element in `map φ T`, they are in `S` and therefore ≤ in `T`.

See also `NatSubgroup.map_le_ NecZero.toNat hj` and `NatSubgroup.map_le__rfl rfl`.
